course: dictionary
lesson: 8931
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer means. Signature has three main meanings: your own name written in your special way, a special feature that makes something easy to recognise, and a sign at the start of music.
explain: «A forged signature on a school note is a serious lie, because it pretends a parent agreed.» Here the clues are forged, note and agreed. Those are about writing your name on a form, so signature means your name written in your own way.
explain: «Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle, a bit like a name.» The dolphins are not writing anything. The whistle makes each dolphin easy to know, so here signature means a special feature that makes something recognisable. Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
fact: A signature is your name written in your own special way.
fact: A signature can also be a special feature that makes something easy to recognise, like a chef's signature dish.
fact: In music, a time signature or key signature is a sign at the start of the music.
fact: When a parent signs a permission slip, the signature shows that they agreed.
fact: Never copy someone else's signature: «A forged signature on a school note is a serious lie.»
exercise: «A forged signature on a school note is a serious lie.» What does signature mean here? | *Your name written in your own way | A loud whistle | A special feature of a dish | A sign at the start of music
exercise: «Each bottlenose dolphin has its own signature whistle, a bit like a name.» What does signature suggest? | A kind of fish | A song played in music | *A special sound that makes one dolphin easy to know | A written name on a form
exercise: Which phrase uses signature to mean a sign at the start of music? | A signature whistle | *A time signature | A signature on the form | A signature dish
test: «Many female sea turtles come back to lay eggs on the beach where they hatched; scientists think they remember its magnetic signature.» What does signature mean here? | A sign at the start of music | A loud noise | A written name | *A special feature that makes the beach easy to recognise
test: Why should you never copy someone else's signature? | Because it makes a loud whistle | Because signatures are only for music | *Because it pretends they agreed, which is a lie | Because it is too hard to write
exam: Mum signs your permission slip, so what does her signature show? | That the slip is very old | *That she agreed to it | That she is a good cook | That the slip is about music
